  {
    "id": "q-physics-ohms-law",
    "thumbnail_intro_seconds": 3,
    "thumbnail": {
      "title": "Ohm's Law",
      "subtitle": "V = IR — Formula · Application · Units",
      "badge": "JEE | NEET | Class 10",
      "topic": "Physics — Electricity",
      "highlights": ["Formula card", "Equation", "Two-column comparison"],
      "style": "dark"
    },
    "meta": {
      "subject": "Physics",
      "topic": "Electricity",
      "subtopic": "Ohm's Law — formula and application",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "exam": "JEE / NEET / Class 10",
      "grade": "Class 10",
      "language": "English"
    },
    "question": {
      "text": "A resistor of 5Ω has a voltage of 15V across it. What is the current through it?",
      "audio": "A resistor of five ohms has a voltage of fifteen volts across it. What is the current through it?",
      "options": [
        { "key": "a", "value": "1 A" },
        { "key": "b", "value": "2 A" },
        { "key": "c", "value": "3 A" },
        { "key": "d", "value": "5 A" }
      ],
      "correct": "c"
    },
    "scenes": [
      {
        "type": "question",
        "text": "A resistor of 5Ω has 15V across it. Find the current.",
        "audio": "A resistor of five ohms has fifteen volts across it. We need to find the current through it. Let us recall Ohm's Law.",
        "render": { "action": "show", "target": "question_block" }
      },
      {
        "type": "options",
        "audio": "Option A one ampere. Option B two ampere. Option C three ampere. Option D five ampere.",
        "render": { "action": "show", "target": "options_grid" }
      },
      {
        "type": "concept",
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "Ohm's Law",
            "audio": "Ohm's Law states that the current through a conductor is directly proportional to the voltage across it and inversely proportional to its resistance.",
            "render": {
              "action": "show",
              "target": "formula_block",
              "value": "V = I × R   →   I = V ÷ R"
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "SI Units",
            "audio": "The SI units: V is voltage in volts, I is current in amperes, R is resistance in ohms.",
            "render": {
              "action": "show",
              "target": "two_col_text",
              "left": {
                "heading": "Symbols",
                "items": ["V = Voltage", "I = Current", "R = Resistance"]
              },
              "right": {
                "heading": "SI Units",
                "items": ["Volt (V)", "Ampere (A)", "Ohm (Ω)"]
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "Substitute values",
            "audio": "Substitute the values. I equals V divided by R. I equals fifteen divided by five.",
            "render": {
              "action": "show",
              "target": "equation",
              "value": "I = V ÷ R = 15 ÷ 5"
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "Current = 3 A",
            "audio": "Fifteen divided by five is three. The current is three amperes. Option C is correct.",
            "render": {
              "action": "show",
              "target": "equation",
              "value": "I = 3 A",
              "highlighted": true
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },

